### Vanexa auth — VS Code REST Client (humeshan pehle server: npm start)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### 1) Register — naya user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "testpass123"
}

### 2) Login — token response body mein aayega (@name se next requests link ho sakti hain)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "testpass123"
}

### 3) Profile GET — login ke baad token cookie mein bhejo (body se copy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
Cookie: token=PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN_RESPONSE_HERE

### 3b) Profile GET — agar REST Client variable use karte ho (login ke turant baad run karo)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
Cookie: token={{login.response.body.token}}

### 4) Profile UPDATE — sirf name / email (JSON)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "name": "Test User Updated",
  "email": "testuser@example.com"
}

### 5) Avatar hataana — removeAvatar
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "removeAvatar": "true"
}

### 6) Password change
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/password/update
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "oldPassword": "testpass123",
  "newPassword": "newpass123",
  "confirmPassword": "newpass123"
}

### 7) Forgot password (email + frontend URL query)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/password/forgot?frontendUrl=http://localhost:5173
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com"
}

###
# Avatar FILE upload Postman / Thunder Client se karo:
#   Method: PUT  {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
#   Auth: Cookie token = (login se token)
#   Body: form-data → avatar = File, optional name/email text fields
###

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/password/reset/PASTE_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "newpass123",
  "confirmPassword": "newpass123"
}